{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>To eat within your gates your grain tithe.</b> He speaks with the Levites and also with Israel regarding the second tithe, according to the majority." "<b>And the firstborn of your cattle and your flock.</b> He speaks with the priests, for the Levites and also the priests are included in [the term] Israel, like ואצו אתכם (Numbers 32:17), where he speaks with the two and a half tribes, and likewise אך פדה תפדה (Deuteronomy 15:19): he speaks with Israel, and the meaning is whoever is obligated to redeem; and likewise לאכול בשעריך לפני ה' אלהיך תאכלנו (Deuteronomy 15:20): whoever is obligated to eat it. The detractors said that these are two firstborns, one the firstborn of the womb and the other the firstborn of the flock, and there is no need to respond to their nonsense. Others said that the firstborn and the tithe are eaten by the Israelite, if he was in the chosen place, and this is the opposite of the verse."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "Resolved the three ellipsed verse citations by context: Numbers 32:17 (ואצו), Deuteronomy 15:19 (פדה), and Deuteronomy 15:20 (תאכלנו)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:17.472493463Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}